# Standards Ansible

## Principes fondamentaux

- **Idempotence** : chaque run produit le même état
- **Déclaratif** : décrire l'état souhaité, pas les étapes
- **Lisible** : YAML clair et documenté

## Structure projet

```
ansible/
├── ansible.cfg
├── requirements.yml          # Collections et rôles externes
├── inventory/
│   ├── production/
│   │   ├── hosts.yml
│   │   ├── group_vars/
│   │   │   ├── all/
│   │   │   │   ├── vars.yml
│   │   │   │   └── vault.yml  # Chiffré
│   │   │   └── webservers.yml
│   │   └── host_vars/
│   └── staging/
├── playbooks/
│   ├── site.yml              # Master playbook
│   ├── webservers.yml
│   └── databases.yml
└── roles/
    └── myapp/
        ├── defaults/main.yml  # Variables par défaut
        ├── vars/main.yml      # Variables internes
        ├── tasks/main.yml
        ├── handlers/main.yml
        ├── templates/
        ├── files/
        └── meta/main.yml      # Dépendances
```

## FQCN obligatoire (Fully Qualified Collection Name)

```yaml
# ❌ MAUVAIS - module non qualifié
- name: Install package
  apt:
    name: nginx

# ✅ BON - FQCN
- name: Install nginx web server
  ansible.builtin.apt:
    name: nginx
    state: present
    update_cache: true
    cache_valid_time: 3600
```

## Nommage des tasks

```yaml
# ❌ MAUVAIS
- name: config
- name: do stuff
- name: nginx

# ✅ BON - Verbe + description claire
- name: Deploy nginx configuration file
- name: Create application directory structure
- name: Ensure nginx service is running and enabled
```

## Template de rôle

```yaml
# roles/myapp/tasks/main.yml
---
- name: Include OS-specific variables
  ansible.builtin.include_vars: "{{ ansible_os_family | lower }}.yml"

- name: Install required packages
  ansible.builtin.package:
    name: "{{ myapp_packages }}"
    state: present
  become: true

- name: Create application user
  ansible.builtin.user:
    name: "{{ myapp_user }}"
    system: true
    shell: /usr/sbin/nologin
    home: "{{ myapp_home }}"
    create_home: true
  become: true

- name: Deploy application configuration
  ansible.builtin.template:
    src: config.yml.j2
    dest: "{{ myapp_config_path }}"
    owner: "{{ myapp_user }}"
    group: "{{ myapp_group }}"
    mode: "0640"
    validate: "{{ myapp_binary }} validate --config %s"
  become: true
  notify: Restart myapp service

- name: Ensure service is running
  ansible.builtin.systemd:
    name: "{{ myapp_service_name }}"
    state: started
    enabled: true
    daemon_reload: true
  become: true
```

## Defaults documentés

```yaml
# roles/myapp/defaults/main.yml
---
# Application settings
myapp_version: "1.0.0"
myapp_user: "myapp"
myapp_group: "myapp"
myapp_home: "/opt/myapp"
myapp_config_path: "/etc/myapp/config.yml"

# Service configuration
myapp_service_name: "myapp"
myapp_port: 8080
myapp_log_level: "info"

# Resource limits
myapp_memory_limit: "512M"
myapp_cpu_limit: "1.0"
```

## Handlers

```yaml
# roles/myapp/handlers/main.yml
---
- name: Restart myapp service
  ansible.builtin.systemd:
    name: "{{ myapp_service_name }}"
    state: restarted
    daemon_reload: true
  become: true

- name: Reload myapp service
  ansible.builtin.systemd:
    name: "{{ myapp_service_name }}"
    state: reloaded
  become: true
```

## Ansible Vault

```bash
# Créer un fichier vault
ansible-vault create group_vars/all/vault.yml

# Éditer
ansible-vault edit group_vars/all/vault.yml

# Exécuter avec vault
ansible-playbook site.yml --ask-vault-pass
ansible-playbook site.yml --vault-password-file ~/.vault_pass
```

```yaml
# group_vars/all/vault.yml (chiffré)
vault_db_password: "supersecret"
vault_api_key: "sk-12345"

# group_vars/all/vars.yml (référence le vault)
db_password: "{{ vault_db_password }}"
api_key: "{{ vault_api_key }}"
```

## Tags pour exécution sélective

```yaml
- name: Deploy web application
  ansible.builtin.import_role:
    name: webapp
  tags:
    - webapp
    - deploy
    - application

- name: Configure monitoring
  ansible.builtin.import_role:
    name: monitoring
  tags:
    - monitoring
    - observability
    - never  # Seulement si explicitement demandé
```

```bash
# Exécuter certains tags
ansible-playbook site.yml --tags "webapp,deploy"

# Exclure des tags
ansible-playbook site.yml --skip-tags "slow,monitoring"

# Lister les tags
ansible-playbook site.yml --list-tags
```

## Check mode et diff

```yaml
# Supporter check mode (dry-run)
- name: Get current version
  ansible.builtin.command: app --version
  register: current_version
  changed_when: false  # Ne marque jamais changed
  check_mode: false    # S'exécute même en check mode

# Afficher les différences
- name: Deploy config
  ansible.builtin.template:
    src: config.j2
    dest: /etc/app/config
  diff: true  # Montre le diff
```

## Checklist Ansible

- [ ] FQCN pour tous les modules
- [ ] Noms de tasks descriptifs (verbe + objet)
- [ ] Permissions explicites (owner, group, mode)
- [ ] Variables dans defaults avec valeurs par défaut
- [ ] Secrets dans Ansible Vault
- [ ] Handlers pour redémarrage services
- [ ] Tags pour exécution granulaire
- [ ] Support du check mode
- [ ] become: true explicite (pas global)
